 CBAutoConfWin args;sz;id;h;w;rows;cols
⍝ Two jobs, keyed by the object id:
⍝  - the button toggles the form size (simulates a window resize), and
⍝  - the grid's Configure event re-deploys its cells to fit the reported size.
 id←⊃args
 :If id≡'F1.BAR.BTN'
     sz←'F1' eWG 'Size'
     :If 460=1⊃sz
         'F1' eWS 'Size' (900 1320)
     :Else
         'F1' eWS 'Size' (460 700)
     :EndIf
 :ElseIf id≡'F1.APP.GRID'
     ⍝ Configure Info = [top left height width]; deploy cells to fit the area.
     h←5⊃args ⋄ w←6⊃args
     rows←3⌈⌊(h-26)÷17     ⍝ minus the column-title band, over the row pitch
     cols←2⌈⌊(w-4)÷90      ⍝ over the (84 + gap) column width
     'F1.APP.GRID' eWS 'Values' ((⍕¨⍳rows)∘.,'/',¨⍕¨⍳cols)
 :EndIf
